  "body": "## Task\n\nBump the pinned `dvdtrsnk/code-review-bot` revision in `.relay/config.yml`\n(`review.bot.ref`) and `.github/workflows/code-review.yml` (the\n`Checkout code-review-bot (private)` step's `ref:`) to\n`b27080ebfeb687e8ec0cb1c76885e96db7f3b22b`.\n\nThat commit fixes a real bug in the cheap-reuse-after-rebase feature shipped\nby the prior pin bump (#491): `check_reuse` gated reuse on the PR's base SHA\nmatching the base SHA recorded at the last verdict, but `merge-pull-request`\nonly re-triggers a review by rebasing onto a base branch that has moved —\nso the base SHA differs on essentially every rebase-triggered re-review,\nmaking the reuse shortcut structurally unreachable in the one scenario it\nexists for. The fix drops the base SHA from the equality gate (diff hash and\nreview-rules hash remain the gate) while still recording it for operator-\nvisible logging. See `dvdtrsnk/code-review-bot#26` for the fix itself.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- `.relay/config.yml`'s `review.bot.ref` is `b27080ebfeb687e8ec0cb1c76885e96db7f3b22b`.\n- `.github/workflows/code-review.yml`'s checkout `ref:` for `dvdtrsnk/code-review-bot` is the same SHA.\n- CI passes, including `code-review` itself (running under the new pin).\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Any other change to the Relay or CI workflow configuration.",
